{"title":"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec79eb0fd4cdd168927d761290bff83ff5405780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 2004 x^2 + mx + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" /> has <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> coefficients and three distinct positive zeros. Exactly one of these is an integer, and it is the sum of the other two.  How many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are possible?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/98625300a750996f07fd03d156018e7f09300e27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 250,\\!000 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 250,\\!250 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 250,\\!500 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 250,\\!750 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 251,\\!000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"594\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the roots be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676589d5a26f8142a0043a695e8cdc964c93f22c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,s,r + s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/9901309ec73ff179b53ef6392e3112dfaaee01e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = rs$\" width=\"47\" height=\"11\" />. Then\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aa6b4356e1b571b8c6b0273d4a5ee73ddd93031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - r)(x - s)(x - (r + s))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f8cb41503afe71a27d8834fd83f6ee33165a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= x^3 - (r + s + r + s) x^2 + (rs + r(r + s) + s(r + s))x - rs(r + s) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"551\" height=\"19\" /></center>\n<p>and by matching coefficients, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/10147b34725735675bfee65a376870ff33e49fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(r + s) = 2004 \\Longrightarrow r + s = 1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" />. Then our polynomial looks like \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb4aa9a18c07d29ec97438dfb06b2f218c49361.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^3 - 2004x^2 + (t + 1002^2)x - 1002t = 0\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"19\" />\nand we need the number of possible products <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aafca7ef8318be6b23bdff9cd67d020839125b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = rs = r(1002 - r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543602db2bcb36cd278f9132792528ef86d5191b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=t+1002^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer, we also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> must be an integer. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22ff7db3e755a8164f2344e0d3d84ea3a0fe93b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d968aec052b8a8f2736faf02fd8fb120489b7cff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/37973f4b2d08d2fc5a2bdd4691b5217eb3336561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; t = r(1002-r) &lt; 501^2 = 251001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"290\" height=\"19\" />, with the endpoints not achievable because the roots must be distinct and positive. Because neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9739d3dba25ae058d11d5f49f4fa6a5100c8c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> can be an integer, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c2dbcb78cd3304be3565ce90b05d63b76f87a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$251,000 - 500 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 250,500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"245\" height=\"28\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/3201d265413f4dadccf88f61e80fd0e1b4e13f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -1002t$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Letting the roots be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c2c80f2b2f8026db5dded79196e8b27ad0b58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = r+s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, we see that by Vieta's Formula's, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c98691102f4a6a513f3f7aa47f30c3293c6d67e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004 = r+s+t = t + t = 2t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"227\" height=\"14\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1c03f2bd028cf11ad7ef50d8025edb79e1f12e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c958cab4df99fef371df0937428b055ec8587dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba9a22e40cb03f955524dbac45dc97540f4e0ea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 2004x^2 + mx + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e2a5d2518cc6fa87f952139f18c1a264c239c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002 \\mid n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b2f98a371d161ccfc3f8c235f64e6eb7ff41fb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1002 \\mid x^3 - 2004x^2 + mx + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"19\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/a/d9a25eec1dc26a3b1d3cc341be0f783831a49a03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -1002a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> and noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055d90246b721383e85d5939b4203b4ea79f06a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 2004x^2 + mx + n = (x-1002)(x^2 - bx + a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"389\" height=\"21\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the sum of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/9667d0ae9aac7eebb09eb7b94d1b9ce3dd443ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - bx + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/853433d5ae7e51b5efcc5b9a9e012889b20bb789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. Now, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f3423c181627885c5ab79b4f9bba6b0ee8c195d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 1002x + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and we wish to find the number of possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. By the quadratic formula, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/910c7c622afd81998d260e3e8d4fe2b7fa178550.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1002 \\pm \\sqrt{1002^2 - 4a}}{2} = 501 \\pm \\sqrt{501^2 - a}\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"40\" /> are the two values of noninteger positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, neither of which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a8720f439e8e8887a0746430412c323e81e13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. This information gives us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f470e0b7901baa5d85b4adad94aef54167c6a8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; 501^2 - a &lt; 501^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"157\" height=\"15\" />, and so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833dbea31aa0e6b7d6cf4b4d803e94997505afc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$501^2 - a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> is evidently not a square, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c87478f40b885ecc0843797566b2a04b8116141.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$501^2 - 1 - 500 = 251,001 - 500 - 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 250,500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"416\" height=\"28\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37b7071ec0f87a7d51318e798725d5d065cbc3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1002a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B\">2004 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195733\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 349/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9361/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.117      1 -total\n 57.82%    8.740      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 40.79%    6.166      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6382:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195733 and revision id 286382. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}